<title>GERMANY: Spar not to take over Krone supermarkets.</title>
<headline>Spar not to take over Krone supermarkets.</headline>
<dateline>SCHENEFELD, Germany 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German supermarket chain Spar Handels AG said on Friday that the supervisory board of Kathreiner AG had rejected its offer to buy 36 Krone stores in the states of Bavaria and Saxony.</p>
<p>Spar said in a regulatory news release that it had offered to buy the stores, which had a combined turnover of 220 million marks a year, not including income tax.</p>
<p>The statement gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
